cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pydemi, please cite it as below."
title: "pydemi: interpretable, fixed-length descriptors from charge-density grids"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-27
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/shubhamkmaurya03/pydemi"
abstract: >-
  pydemi turns volumetric charge densities, from DFT calculations or predicted
  by machine-learning models from the crystal structure, into named,
  fixed-length vectors of physically interpretable descriptors in five domains
  (bonding, structural, magnetic, site heterogeneity and composition), each
  registered with its formula, units, range, degenerate-case values and
  stability.
keywords:
  - charge density
  - density-functional theory
  - materials descriptors
  - featurization
  - materials informatics
  - VASP
authors:
  - family-names: Maurya
    given-names: Shubham Kumar
    affiliation: "CMS Lab, Department of Materials Science & Engineering, Indian Institute of Technology Kanpur"
  - family-names: Bhowmick
    given-names: Somnath
    affiliation: "Department of Materials Science & Engineering, Indian Institute of Technology Kanpur"
